  "facts": [
    "The Fremont Bridge, a steel tied‑arch marvel, boasts the longest main span in Oregon at 902 feet, making it the second longest tied‑arch bridge worldwide after China’s Caiyuanba Bridge.",
    "On March 16, 1973, the bridge’s 6,000‑short‑ton steel arch was hoisted 170 feet by 32 hydraulic jacks, earning a Guinness World Record for the heaviest lift ever completed at that time.",
    "Designed with public input, the Fremont Bridge cost nearly six times more than the Marquam Bridge, reflecting a commitment to aesthetic quality that earned it a place in the 1975 Portland Art Commission’s vision."
